#{[17592186414497 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186414492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414497 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73613" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414497 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414497 #edb/ref 1071 "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414497 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ef768962-c254-565f-ad90-7c7187cd37b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186414497 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column." #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
